{"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"targets SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}]},{"text":" — computed properties, ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-four-rules","level":2,"text":"The four rules","type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"computed property \/ expression","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gesture + "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@GestureState"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" body. Origami ","type":"text"},{"code":"Transition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".transition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier — that’s a different concept).","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property","level":3,"text":"Pure value patch → computed property","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition\/interpolate"},{"type":"text","text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property (or an inline expression) — no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", no side effect."}]},{"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","level":3,"text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose output lands in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture arbitration clean.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","level":3,"text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sample and Hold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","type":"heading","text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"type":"text","text":", and other animation patches drive a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier on the animated property."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","type":"heading","text":"Flag, don’t fake","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"]}],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","title":"Beats","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"title":"Drag","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"abstract":[{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drag"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" patch (","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" patch."}],"type":"topic","title":"Interaction","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"title":"Swami","kind":"symbol"}}}